  "intro": "<p><b>CSEC Information Technology · Paper 02 · Mock 1</b> · 2 hours · 90 marks</p><ol><li>This paper consists of <b>FOUR</b> compulsory structured questions. Answer <b>ALL</b> questions.</li><li>Marks: Question 1 (20), Question 2 (25), Question 3 (20), Question 4 (25). Plan about 1⅓ minutes per mark: 25 minutes for a 20-mark question and 33 minutes for a 25-mark question, with 10 minutes to check.</li><li>Each question is built around one Caribbean scenario and mixes theory (Sections 1–3), productivity tools (Sections 4–6) and problem-solving and programming (Sections 7–8).</li><li>Label every part (a), (b), (i), (ii). Use the command word: <i>state</i>, <i>list</i> and <i>identify</i> need short answers; <i>describe</i>, <i>explain</i>, <i>distinguish</i>, <i>justify</i> and <i>evaluate</i> need developed points linked to the scenario.</li><li>Type formulas exactly as you would enter them (e.g. <code>=SUM(B2:B9)</code>), query criteria as they would appear in the design grid, and code with indentation. Programs may be written in Python, Pascal or Visual Basic (VBA), the languages CXC accepts.</li><li>Stuck? Use <b>Dial it down</b> for a scaffolded version of a question, or <b>Grade One challenge</b> to stretch yourself after you finish.</li></ol><p class=\"tip\">This is an original mock paper written in the format of the CXC CSEC Information Technology Paper 02 (syllabus CXC 30/G/SYLL 17).</p>",
