    "stimulus": "<p>The Bahamas is hosting the <b>Caribbean Youth Games 2026</b>. The organising committee has an office in Nassau with 20 computers, a media centre at the Thomas A. Robinson National Stadium 3 km away, and a results desk at each of four venues across the island. Athletes from 14 countries will register on the Games website before they travel.</p><p>The committee's IT officer, Ms. Sheranne Rolle, must link the sites, launch the website and keep athlete data safe.</p>",
    "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li><b>(i)</b> Identify the type of network that would link the 20 computers in the Nassau office, and the type that would link the office, the media centre and the four venues. <i>(2 marks)</i> <b>(ii)</b> State the function of a <b>switch</b> and of a <b>router</b> in the committee's network. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>The link between the office and the media centre must carry live HD video of events. <b>Recommend</b> a transmission medium and justify your choice by comparing it with ONE other medium. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>The home page of the Games website must have: the Games logo at the top, a navigation bar linking to <i>Schedule</i>, <i>Results</i> and <i>Register</i> pages, a link to e-mail <code>media@cyg2026.bs</code>, and a link that jumps to the <i>Venues</i> section lower on the same page. <b>(i)</b> Write the HTML for the logo (with alternative text), ONE navigation link, the e-mail link and the same-page link with its target. <i>(5 marks)</i> <b>(ii)</b> State TWO design features (other than those listed) that would make the site easy to use on a phone. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Athletes enter their name, date of birth, passport number and medical details on the Register page. <b>(i)</b> Explain how a <b>phishing</b> attack could target the athletes, and the effect on them. <i>(3 marks)</i> <b>(ii)</b> Describe THREE countermeasures the committee should use to protect the registration data, including ONE physical and ONE software measure. <i>(6 marks)</i></li><li>Explain why the committee should use <b>HTTPS</b> rather than HTTP for the Register page. <i>(1 mark)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>[25 marks]</b></p>",
