    "genre": "Paper 02 Question 3 · SOs 5.3, 5.4, 5.5, 5.7, 5.8, 6.2, 6.3, 6.4 (20 marks)",
    "stimulus": "<p><b>Bayside Hardware</b> in Charlestown sells building supplies. The manager, Mr. Romney, keeps weekly sales in a spreadsheet:</p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th><th>D</th><th>E</th><th>F</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>1</th><td colspan=\"4\"><b>Bayside Hardware · weekly sales</b></td><td>Discount rate</td><td>5%</td></tr><tr><th>2</th><td><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Item</b></td><td><b>Unit price ($)</b></td><td><b>Qty sold</b></td><td><b>Sales ($)</b></td><td><b>Restock?</b></td></tr><tr><th>3</th><td>P101</td><td>Plywood sheet</td><td>38.50</td><td>42</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>4</th><td>C220</td><td>Cement bag</td><td>14.75</td><td>130</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>5</th><td>N015</td><td>Box of nails</td><td>6.20</td><td>18</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>6</th><td>H310</td><td>Hurricane strap</td><td>3.95</td><td>260</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>7</th><td>T088</td><td>Tarpaulin</td><td>22.00</td><td>9</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>8</th><td></td><td><b>Total</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>He also wants a database with two tables: <b>Suppliers</b> (SupplierID, SupplierName, Island, Phone) and <b>Products</b> (Code, Item, UnitPrice, InStock, SupplierID).</p>",
    "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>Write the formula for cell <b>E3</b> to calculate Sales as Unit price × Qty sold, and the formula for <b>E8</b> to total the sales. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Mr. Romney wants a column G showing the discounted sales, using the discount rate in F1. <b>(i)</b> Write the formula for <b>G3</b> so that it can be copied down to G7. <i>(2 marks)</i> <b>(ii)</b> Explain why your formula needs an absolute reference. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Write the formula for <b>F3</b> that displays \"Yes\" if fewer than 20 were sold and \"No\" otherwise. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>State the function that would find the item with the highest quantity sold value, writing the formula for D9. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Mr. Romney wants a chart comparing the Sales of the five items. Name the most suitable chart type and state TWO labels the chart should have. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li><b>(i)</b> Identify the primary key of each database table and the foreign key. <i>(3 marks)</i> <b>(ii)</b> State the type of relationship between Suppliers and Products. <i>(1 mark)</i> <b>(iii)</b> Suggest a suitable data type for UnitPrice and for InStock. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Describe a query to list the Item, UnitPrice and SupplierName of every product supplied from <b>Trinidad</b> with a UnitPrice above $10, sorted by Item. State the tables, fields and criteria. <i>(4 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>[20 marks]</b></p>",
    "min": 120,
