    "bloom": "Analyse",
    "genre": "Paper 02 Question 1 · SOs 1.3, 1.6, 1.10, 1.11, 1.13, 1.14, 1.15 (20 marks)",
    "stimulus": "<p>After a Category 4 hurricane, <b>Relief CAY</b>, a non-profit in West Bay, gives food and building materials to households. Volunteers carry paper <b>registration forms</b> door to door. Each form has boxes for the household's name, address, district, number of people, and tick boxes for needs (food, water, roofing, medicine). Back at the office, the forms are entered into a computer, and each household is given a printed <b>voucher</b> with a barcode. When the household collects supplies, the voucher is scanned and the clerk writes the items collected on the voucher, which is then scanned back in.</p><p>Some of the office laptops were damaged by flooding, and the volunteer co-ordinator, Mr. Hodge, has asked for your help.</p>",
    "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li><b>Distinguish</b> between data and information, using an example from Relief CAY. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li><b>(i)</b> Identify the source document in the scenario. <i>(1 mark)</i> <b>(ii)</b> Explain why the voucher is a <b>turnaround document</b>. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Relief CAY wants to stop typing the tick-box needs by hand. <b>Name</b> a suitable input device and <b>explain</b> how it would work with the forms. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>For each field below, name a suitable validation check and give ONE example of data it would reject: <b>(i)</b> Number of people (1 to 20); <b>(ii)</b> District (must be one of the island's districts); <b>(iii)</b> Household name. <i>(6 marks)</i></li><li>The household file is stored on a server. Most of the time a clerk must find ONE household quickly when a voucher is scanned; at the end of each week a full report is printed in household-number order. <b>Recommend</b> a file organisation method and justify it. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>One laptop that was in the flood now switches on, but the screen stays black and the fan is very loud. <b>Outline</b> THREE troubleshooting steps a volunteer should take, in a sensible order. <i>(3 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>[20 marks]</b></p>",
    "min": 180,
