    "stimulus": "<p><b>Caribbean Health Connect</b> is a telemedicine service linking clinics in Anguilla, St. Kitts and Montserrat with specialist doctors in Barbados. Patients book video consultations on a smartphone app, and nurses send readings from wearable devices. The service also e-mails monthly health newsletters and appointment letters to 2,400 patients.</p><p>Last month, staff received e-mails that looked as if they came from the IT department asking them to \"confirm your password\". Two staff replied, and patient records were later posted online.</p>",
    "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li><b>Explain</b> TWO ways in which mobile communication technologies support the telemedicine service. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>State TWO problems patients in rural areas of the islands may face when using the app. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li><b>(i)</b> Name the type of attack described in the scenario. <i>(1 mark)</i> <b>(ii)</b> Discuss ONE impact of the data leak on the PATIENTS and ONE impact on the ORGANISATION. <i>(4 marks)</i> <b>(iii)</b> Recommend TWO measures to stop a repeat, other than antivirus software. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>Name the IT professional who would be responsible for <b>(i)</b> deciding which staff may view which patient records and maintaining the database, and <b>(ii)</b> monitoring the network for attacks. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>The 2,400 appointment letters are produced by mail merge. <b>(i)</b> Name the TWO files needed and state what each contains. <i>(2 marks)</i> <b>(ii)</b> Explain how the clinic could send letters ONLY to patients in St. Kitts. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>The 30-page staff handbook needs a table of contents that updates automatically. Describe the TWO steps needed. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Telemedicine has reduced the number of patients flown to Barbados. State ONE benefit and ONE drawback of telemedicine for the region. <i>(2 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>[25 marks]</b></p>",
