    "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>Write formulas for: <b>(i)</b> E2, the total of the three scores; <b>(ii)</b> F2, the average of the three scores, rounded to 1 decimal place; <b>(iii)</b> G2, the rank of the contestant's total among all five (highest = 1), that can be copied down to G6. <i>(5 marks)</i></li><li>Explain why the range in your RANK formula must be absolute. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>The organisers want the five rows sorted so the winner is at the top. State the sort key and the order. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>A summary sheet named <b>Results</b> must show the winning total from the Scores sheet. Write a formula for cell B2 on Results that finds the highest total on the Scores sheet. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>State TWO formatting features that would make the sheet easier to read for the judges. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li><b>(i)</b> State the primary key of each table and identify the foreign key. <i>(2 marks)</i> <b>(ii)</b> Suggest a validation rule for Section, which may only be VIP, Grandstand or Bleachers. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Write the criteria (as they would appear in Query Design) for a query that lists the names of patrons who bought <b>VIP</b> tickets for the show on <b>25/04/2026</b>. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>State the purpose of a <b>main form with a subform</b> in this database and say which table belongs in each part. <i>(3 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>[20 marks]</b></p>",
