    "model": "<p><b>(a)(i)</b> E2: <code>=SUM(B2:D2)</code> <b>(ii)</b> F2: <code>=ROUND(AVERAGE(B2:D2),1)</code> <b>(iii)</b> G2: <code>=RANK(E2,$E$2:$E$6)</code> (or <code>=RANK.EQ(E2,$E$2:$E$6,0)</code>). Totals: 70, 70, 72, 69, 68, so Miss Belize City ranks 1, Miss San Ignacio and Miss Dangriga tie on 2.</p><p><b>(b)</b> When G2 is copied down, a relative range would shift to E3:E7, E4:E8 … and would leave out contestants at the top; $E$2:$E$6 keeps the comparison range fixed.</p><p><b>(c)</b> Primary sort key: Total, in descending order (largest first).</p><p><b>(d)</b> <code>=MAX(Scores!E2:E6)</code> (returns 72).</p><p><b>(e)</b> Bold, shaded column headings; conditional formatting that highlights the highest total in gold (also: borders, freeze the top row, one decimal place for averages).</p><p><b>(f)(i)</b> Patrons: PatronID. Tickets: TicketNo. PatronID in Tickets is the foreign key linking to Patrons. <b>(ii)</b> Validation rule: <code>\"VIP\" Or \"Grandstand\" Or \"Bleachers\"</code> with validation text \"Choose VIP, Grandstand or Bleachers\".</p><p><b>(g)</b> Use both tables, joined on PatronID:</p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><tr><th>Field</th><td>FirstName</td><td>LastName</td><td>Section</td><td>ShowDate</td></tr><tr><th>Table</th><td>Patrons</td><td>Patrons</td><td>Tickets</td><td>Tickets</td></tr><tr><th>Show</th><td>✔</td><td>✔</td><td>☐</td><td>☐</td></tr><tr><th>Criteria</th><td></td><td></td><td>\"VIP\"</td><td>#25/04/2026#</td></tr></table></div><p>Both criteria are on the same row (AND).</p><p><b>(h)</b> A main form with a subform shows one record and its related records together, so staff can look up a patron and see or add all the tickets that patron bought in one screen. Main form: Patrons. Subform: Tickets (linked by PatronID).</p>",
    "key": "<p><b>Mark scheme</b></p><ul><li>(a)(i) SUM formula (1). (ii) AVERAGE (1) with ROUND to 1 dp (1). (iii) RANK of E2 (1) with absolute range (1).</li><li>(b) Reason (1).</li><li>(c) Total descending (1).</li><li>(d) Sheet reference Scores! (1); MAX of E2:E6 (1).</li><li>(e) Any two suitable features (1 each).</li><li>(f)(i) Both PKs (1), FK (1). (ii) Rule (1).</li><li>(g) \"VIP\" in Section (1); date in ShowDate with # or correct format (1); on the same row / both tables used (1).</li><li>(h) Purpose (1); Patrons main (1); Tickets sub (1).</li></ul>",
