    "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>Using top-down design, break the problem into THREE sub-tasks. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Write pseudocode for the algorithm. Use an array <code>runs[1..8]</code> and a FOR loop. <i>(8 marks)</i></li><li>Draw (describe in words) the flowchart symbol you would use for: <b>(i)</b> reading runs; <b>(ii)</b> testing whether runs ≥ 30; <b>(iii)</b> adding runs to the total. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Complete a trace table for the FIRST FOUR batters only, with the data <b>12, 45, 30, 7</b>. Show total, highest and bonusCount. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>A student types <code>for i in range(1, 8):</code> to read all 8 scores into a Python list. <b>(i)</b> Explain what is wrong and what type of error it is. <b>(ii)</b> Write the corrected line. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li><b>(i)</b> Python is translated by an interpreter. State ONE difference between an interpreter and a compiler. <b>(ii)</b> Give TWO examples of internal documentation the student should include in the program. <i>(4 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>[25 marks]</b></p>",
