    "model": "<p><b>(a) Primary document: ResultsLetter</b></p><div class=\"passage\"><p style=\"text-align:center\"><b>NATIONAL YOUTH ELECTORAL COMMISSION</b><br>12 Bay Street, Kingstown, St. Vincent and the Grenadines · info@nyec.vc</p><p>20 May 2026</p><p>«FirstName» «LastName»<br>«School»</p><p>Dear «FirstName»,</p><p><b>Invitation to Results Night</b></p><p>Congratulations on standing as a candidate for the <b>«Constituency»</b> constituency in the 2026 National Youth Parliament Elections. The Commission invites you to Results Night on <b>Thursday 28 May 2026 at 7:00 p.m.</b> at the St. Vincent and the Grenadines Youth Centre, where the results for every constituency will be announced.</p><p>Please arrive by 6:30 p.m. and bring your student ID. One parent or guardian may attend with you. Kindly confirm by e-mail to info@nyec.vc by 25 May.</p><p>Yours sincerely,<br><br>Naomi Cato-Carty<br>Chief Youth Electoral Officer</p></div><p>Steps: Mailings ▸ Start Mail Merge ▸ Letters; Select Recipients ▸ Use an Existing List ▸ <b>Candidates.csv</b>; Insert Merge Field for FirstName, LastName, School, Constituency; date inserted with Insert ▸ Date &amp; Time.</p><p><b>(b)</b> Edit Recipient List ▸ Filter ▸ Field: <b>Constituency</b>, Comparison: <b>Equal to</b>, Compare to: <b>Layou</b>. Preview shows 3 recipients. Finish &amp; Merge ▸ Edit Individual Documents ▸ All, saved as <code>LayouLetters</code>. Letters produced for: <b>Kemar Hazel (Hummingbird Ridge High School), Tia Ollivierre (Flamboyant Heights College), Jaylen DaSilva (Calabash Point Secondary)</b>.</p><p><b>(c) PollingAgentForm</b></p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Prompt</th><th>Control</th><th>Settings</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Full name</td><td>Plain-text content control</td><td>Placeholder: Click to type your full name</td></tr><tr><td>School</td><td>Drop-down list</td><td>Hummingbird Ridge High School; Flamboyant Heights College; Calabash Point Secondary; Other</td></tr><tr><td>Constituency</td><td>Drop-down list</td><td>Kingstown; Georgetown; Layou; Barrouallie</td></tr><tr><td>Date of birth</td><td>Date picker</td><td>Format dd/MM/yyyy</td></tr><tr><td>I agree to follow the NYEC code of conduct</td><td>Check box</td><td>Unticked by default</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Protection: Review ▸ Restrict Editing ▸ Editing restrictions: <b>Filling in forms</b> ▸ Yes, Start Enforcing Protection (optional password). The labels can no longer be changed; only the controls can be completed.</p>",
