     "prompt": "<p>Create the home page <code>index.html</code> of the NYEC website <b>Vote Youth SVG</b>. It must contain:</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>A logo image at the top (any image named <code>nyec-logo.png</code>) with suitable alternative text, and the heading <b>Vote Youth SVG 2026</b>. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>A navigation bar with links to two other pages, <code>candidates.html</code> and <code>howtovote.html</code>. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>A hyperlink that opens an e-mail to <code>info@nyec.vc</code>. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>A hyperlink to the file <code>PollingAgentForm.docx</code> you created in Question 1. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>A section headed <b>Key dates</b> lower on the page, and a link at the top that jumps to it. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>A consistent design: page title, readable font, colour scheme and a footer. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Add a table on <code>candidates.html</code> listing the three Layou candidates with columns Name, Party and School, with a caption. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Evaluate your home page against TWO website evaluation criteria (e.g. usability, accessibility, display on phones, load time) and describe ONE change you would make. <i>(2 marks)</i></li></ol><p>Paste your HTML (or describe each element if you used a website builder) in the answer box.</p><p class=\"row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn ghost\" data-gx=\"opengame\" data-page=\"games/websim.html?level=3\" data-id=\"websim\">🌐 Open the Web Page Builder</button> <span class=\"hint\">Build it in the Web Page Builder and switch to Code view to copy your HTML.</span></p>",
