    "prompt": "<p>Open <b>PollingStations.csv</b> so the headings are in row 1 and the data in rows 2–9. Save the workbook as <code>Turnout</code>. In cell <b>J2</b> type <i>Target turnout</i> and in <b>K2</b> enter <b>75%</b>.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>In F1 type <i>ValidVotes</i>, G1 <i>Turnout</i>, H1 <i>TargetMet</i>. In F2 enter a formula for the valid votes (ballots cast minus rejected). In G2 enter a formula for turnout (ballots cast ÷ registered), formatted as a percentage with 1 decimal place. Copy both down to row 9. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>In H2 enter a formula that displays <b>Yes</b> if the turnout is at least the target in K2 and <b>No</b> otherwise. It must use an absolute reference so it can be copied to H9. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>In row 10 type <i>Total</i> and use functions to total columns C, D, E and F. In G11 find the highest turnout, and in H11 count how many stations did NOT meet the target. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Sort the station rows (2–9) by Turnout, highest first. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Create a column chart of Turnout for each Station, with the title <b>Youth Parliament 2026 Turnout by Polling Station</b> and axis titles. Place it on a new sheet named <b>TurnoutChart</b>. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Copy the data to a sheet named <b>BelowTarget</b> and use a filter to show only the stations where TargetMet is No. <i>(1 mark)</i></li></ol><p>In the answer box, type every formula exactly as entered, the results you got, and how you did the sort, chart and filter.</p><p class=\"row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn ghost\" data-gx=\"opengame\" data-page=\"games/excelsim.html?level=3\" data-id=\"excelsim\">🟩 Open the Excel Lab</button> <span class=\"hint\">Import PollingStations.csv with File ▸ Open.</span></p>",
