    "prompt": "<p>At each small polling station, ballots for three candidates are counted by computer. Each ballot is entered as the candidate's number: <b>1</b>, <b>2</b> or <b>3</b>. Any other number (except 0) is a <b>spoilt</b> ballot. Entering <b>0</b> ends the count, and the program must stop after a <b>maximum of 8</b> ballots even if 0 has not been entered. The program must output the votes for each candidate, the number of spoilt ballots and the number of the winning candidate (or \"No clear winner\" if the highest count is shared).</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>Write a problem statement and list the inputs, processing and outputs. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Write pseudocode (or draw a flowchart) for the algorithm. Your loop must stop on 0 OR after 8 ballots. <i>(5 marks)</i></li><li>Complete a trace table for the data <b>2, 1, 2, 5, 3, 2, 0</b>. Show vote, count, c1, c2, c3, spoilt and the output. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Write the program in Python (Pascal is acceptable). Save it as <code>BallotCounter</code>. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>Run your program with the test data in (c) and record the output. <i>(1 mark)</i></li></ol><p class=\"row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn ghost\" data-gx=\"opengame\" data-page=\"games/codelab.html?level=3\" data-id=\"codelab\">🐍 Open the Code Lab</button> <span class=\"hint\">Use the pseudocode interpreter, trace table tool and Python editor.</span></p>",
