    "prompt": "<p>Open <b>BoothSales.csv</b> (headings in row 1, data in rows 2–11) and save the workbook as <code>BoothSales</code>. In K2 type <i>Weekly rent</i> and in L2 enter <b>350</b>; in K3 type <i>Commission rate</i> and in L3 enter <b>10%</b>.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>In G1:J1 type the headings TotalSales, Charges, Net and Status. In G2 use a function to total the three weeks. In H2 calculate the charges: three weeks of rent plus the commission on TotalSales, using absolute references to L2 and L3. In I2 calculate Net (TotalSales minus Charges). Copy the formulas to row 11 and format G:I as currency with 2 decimal places. <i>(4 marks)</i></li><li>In J2 enter a formula that displays <b>Gold vendor</b> if Net is $3,000 or more and <b>Standard</b> otherwise. Copy to J11. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>In G12 find the average TotalSales, in G13 the highest TotalSales and in J12 the number of Gold vendors. <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>Sort rows 2–11 by FoodType (A to Z) and then by TotalSales (largest first). <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Create a bar or column chart of TotalSales by Vendor titled <b>Carnival Village 2026 Food Booth Sales</b>, with axis titles, on a new sheet named <b>SalesChart</b>. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>On a copy of the data named <b>Drinks</b>, filter to show only booths whose FoodType is Drinks. <i>(1 mark)</i></li></ol><p>Record every formula, your results and how you sorted, charted and filtered.</p><p class=\"row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn ghost\" data-gx=\"opengame\" data-page=\"games/excelsim.html?level=3\" data-id=\"excelsim\">🟩 Open the Excel Lab</button> <span class=\"hint\">Import BoothSales.csv with File ▸ Open.</span></p>",
